# Feature: drop zone (Phase 9)

Library screen `#dropzone`: drop WAV files or folders. Renderer uses `pathForFile` + `statPath`. Only directories and `.wav`/`.wave` files are sent to Python. The drop zone can be closed for more library space; `#app-bar` **Show drop zone** / **Hide drop zone** (and Close on the drop zone) toggles it. `#app-bar` also has a logo placeholder and **Settings**, which opens the shared `#dialog` (empty for now).

`classify_and_ingest {paths}` moves tagged originals into `libraryRoot`. The same method is used when the user reclassifies files already in the library. First analyze can be slow (YAMNet load). Disable further drops while `ingesting`. After the job, set `ingesting = false` **before** `refresh()` so Reclassify / Re-run YAMNet enable again.

`#ingest-jobs` lists per-file status from progress events (`inspect` → `analyze` → `tag` → `move` → `done`/`error`) and the final job results (`→ Pour` or error text). The list sits in `#ingest-panel` under the drop zone; **Close** hides it after the job (disabled while ingesting). Then `list_library` refresh. Dragging library files out of Fieldy must not re-ingest them if they are dropped back on `#dropzone`.

Prevent window default drag/drop so Chromium does not navigate. Python still walks folders for WAV; non-WAV inside a folder is skipped by ingest expand.

